edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278103 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278103 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278103 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278103 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278103 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186277243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278103 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d6dfb508-76d9-5717-9115-0d19ca58e6d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278149 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278149 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278149 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278149 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278149 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278149 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278149 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278149 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186276518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278149 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f088e059-56d3-5859-8349-448073079bbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278168 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278168 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278168 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278168 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278168 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278168 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278168 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278168 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186277236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278168 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fb0ee147-a553-542c-8e10-1d6e3f554db7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278550 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278550 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161548" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278550 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278550 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,-3\\le x\\le 5{y}^{4}+2},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $yz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278550 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "587a8773-2afe-542a-990e-6aafa5beb6ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278550 #edb/ref 1074 "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1b49704bf6d5837a18d8b5dbb8b420d430d5e3881507540fb62a45cf1f6ce52f.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-3\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)=5{y}^{4}+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278554 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278554 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161561" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278554 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278554 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}4xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{4-2y}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278554 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a2982d5e-855b-5753-9807-1b56cd50c77d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278554 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}4xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}[2z{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2z({z}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2y}}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{4-2y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{4-2y)})^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(4-2y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(16-16y+4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8-8y+2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[8y-4{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =16-16+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278556 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278556 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161564" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278556 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278556 #edb/ref 1071 "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-z\\le y\\le 1,\\,4\\le z\\le 5,\\,-\\sqrt{y+z}\\le x\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278556 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4ac74bdd-4f55-52a9-8415-18543bfb88ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278556 #edb/ref 1074 "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/a9/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-\\sqrt{y+z},\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-z\\le y\\le 1,\\,4\\le z\\le 5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{4}^{5}{\\int }_{-z}^{1}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dy\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{5}{\\int }_{-z}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=4+5=9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278557 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278557 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161566" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278557 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278557 #edb/ref 1071 "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-8\\le y\\le {sin}^{2}⁡z,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi ,\\,-2y-1\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+2z}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278557 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "29632302-5883-5021-9de6-855ebf0325c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278557 #edb/ref 1074 "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/a9/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-2y-1,\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)={y}^{2}+2z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-8\\le y\\le {sin}^{2}⁡z,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-8}^{{sin}^{2}⁡z}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dy\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-8}^{{sin}^{2}⁡z}{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=0+\\pi =\\pi .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278565 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278565 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161583" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278565 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278565 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le yz},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the parabola $z={y}^{2}$ in the first quadrant." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278565 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40c7ad15-9d9f-5fe8-85c1-e6adcf3df389" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278565 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{yz}2x\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{yz}2x\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=yz}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(yz)^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/ac/acb173db9d28ed8b38e63c7bc365c20e5755aeb1af3f6340e7b9229a4b49101d.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z={y}^{2}}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}({y}^{6}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{8}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{1}{9}{y}^{9}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{9}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278566 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278566 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161585" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278566 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278566 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the parabola $z=-{y}^{2}$ in the fourth quadrant." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278566 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a816d812-5042-53f7-abc8-46b6718aff74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278566 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}[x]_{x=0}^{x={y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/38/38ea49a6fae41574107b2ba68a578586a306cf43d419d4de5699dcfa009137c2.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{0}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{0}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[({y}^{2}+1)z+\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=-{y}^{2}}^{z=0}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}+1)((0-(-{y}^{2}))+\\frac{1}{3}(0-{(-{y}^{2})}^{3})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}+1){y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{4}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{5}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{21}{y}^{7}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{61}{105}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278567 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278567 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161589" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278567 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278567 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d5/d5690bff5819d72cc9d49016c119dc79f62f4d766c142a43a89df196ce9f2335.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278567 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5d288958-0f39-531c-abbd-563a70ab640a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278567 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/24/2427e053c0e2d808b32db5d7fedf81365e7e50f0b3f2dc61598ad1795394686e.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/14/145f0d494ffe24de84e3a289b3a7316d3f4933f193d734aed118609f7fb9f94f.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2+2y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}(2+2y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{y}^{2}z+2{y}^{3}z-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,dy & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279007 #edb/ref 1080 "12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279007 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279007 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2f863192-f157-5fb8-942d-593165f6be17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279138 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279138 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279138 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3e0a52c4-85e6-5e49-87e7-389cbb36adbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279330 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279330 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279330 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "50f21f17-6e6a-547f-9424-2ed97e19e1ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279386 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279386 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279386 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56db55ba-db05-567a-9988-071184b844d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279543 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279543 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279543 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "688f55f5-366d-5010-ab2b-a189e5f23bc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279848 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279848 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279848 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8cf90354-3814-59d5-a7cf-c0bc9a3254d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279956 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279956 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186279956 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9a3de7a1-dfce-5742-8880-f5852e9d512f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280390 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280390 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280390 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ccc2f76c-4d6a-5867-b8af-3f6282d7d40f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280724 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280724 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280724 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f3a47d8f-8a5c-5150-8c7d-8102990223cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280807 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{9}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280807 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280807 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fd1c3683-c4dd-5443-82b2-d8994d7dbb7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281038 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281038 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281038 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281038 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281038 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281038 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281038 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281038 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186279138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281038 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "736232dd-927d-57e3-adc3-ed1ba5cd49e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281048 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281048 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281048 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186279543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281048 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7566d184-eeca-5394-8d91-0aadcdbc31b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281323 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281323 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161783" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281323 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281323 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/3f/3fe3ec24f8f8006f22bde8ba2dc39fd3cd3f73668b06f8ea4a74e4ed5206a193.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281323 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "90f67d54-9024-5f72-8cbf-c5f497fb6e8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281323 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/2a/2a20f2651c24e48871028b44fe61da4600d632481877ef32ccdfd3241262a53b.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 5-y-\\frac{z}{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1ba7c02f254313a73a813e4e43c44c25523ce77dd47e594a1db3b412a6bd5c3d.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 5-y-\\frac{z}{2}}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=5-y-z/2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}(5-y-\\frac{z}{2})\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{z}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=4}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\,dy & =[2y]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =6-0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161784" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ca/ca49b92d602d04a73dc7ab9936d601654bd293ce3fb7950372ac86155875aca3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "78eec2a4-7ee5-59eb-8402-37f965ae8bd1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/00/0008ba406cfe8a5b61d683a6854260897cb441752a5333add281ab1279e31b0b.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{y}{3}+z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/bb/bbe6b6b897e5d53421080ae8e8b9dc49f2ea1b7e135f8426ee3f11af01cc2401.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le 2-\\frac{y}{3}+z}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2-y/3+z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}(2-\\frac{y}{3}+z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{[z]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}(3)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dy & =[y]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
